  -  Known and unfixed (#NNN): `JobSnapshot.elapsed` is `started_at.elapsed()` at snapshot time, so a *finished* job's duration keeps growing on every `/bg list`.
  +  Day 165 (#736): a finished job's elapsed time is **frozen**, not recomputed — `BackgroundJob.runtime` (`Arc<Mutex<Option<Duration>>>`) is stamped once at completion by *every* writer that marks a job finished (normal exit, spawn failure, and `kill`, all via the shared `stamp_runtime`), and `list` reads `runtime.unwrap_or_else(|| started_at.elapsed())`, so only a still-running job reads the live clock. Before this, `/bg list` rendered `started_at.elapsed()` unconditionally and a job that took 0.2s read `✓ done 1h3m` an hour later — the number a user reads as "how long that build took" was "how long ago I started it". The abstention case has its own value rather than borrowing the convenient neighbour: `JobSnapshot.runtime` stays `Option`, and `elapsed_column` prints `--` (`UNKNOWN_ELAPSED`) for a job that is finished but never stamped a runtime (reachable: `finished` is a `Relaxed` store, so a reader can see the flag before the stamp) instead of presenting the live clock as a runtime. `format_elapsed` is unchanged — the formatter was always fine, its input wasn't.
