Done. #736 is fixed and committed.

What changed (src/commands_bg.rs, one file + the CLAUDE.md bullet):

• `BackgroundJob.runtime: Arc<Mutex<Option<Duration>>> — stamped once at completion through a shared stamp_runtime` helper.
• Writer set, verified by grep rather than recall — there were three, not the two the task predicted: run_background_command's normal exit, its spawn-failure early return (stores finished and returns before the wait path), and kill. All three stamp before flipping finished.
• list() → elapsed: runtime.unwrap_or_else(|| j.started_at.elapsed()), so only a running job reads the live clock.
• **Abstention has its own value**: JobSnapshot.runtime stays Option, and a new elapsed_column prints -- for finished-but-unstamped. That state is genuinely reachable — finished is a `Relaxed` store, so a reader can observe the flag before the mutex-guarded stamp — so I rendered it honestly rather than claiming unreachability.
• format_elapsed untouched, its existing tests untouched.

Tests (written first, watched fail): running elapsed still grows; finished elapsed is byte-identical across two list() calls separated by a real 400 ms sleep (the "elapsed is small" version would have passed on the buggy code); killed job likewise; and the unstamped-finished string asserted at the emission point.

